// Goéland POC - Organizational units (spec v2 §5.7, §31).
//
// Proto-first definition for OrgUnitService + supporting messages. An
// organizational unit (direction, service, office, ...) is an internal unit of
// the administration, never an ACTOR: a first-class subject (kind = ORG_UNIT)
// in one tree, that cases, tasks and circulations target through typed
// relationships (CASE_HAS_ORG_UNIT_LEADER, _MANAGER, _PARTICIPANT) and that
// RecordMetadata.owner_org_id names.
//
// Units have no natural unique code: the abbreviation (sigle) is often shared
// with the parent unit. Identity is the subject id; live siblings never share
// a label. A unit is never deleted: it is dissolved with a reason and stays as history.
// Reading requires goeland:read; every mutation requires goeland:admin and is
// audited in the same transaction.

